From f4edd107899c9832f5266d8b818df102a34dc9c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 23:17:05 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1150/1157] fix(kanban): worker-node capability routing relays
 to the card's home gateway [daveey]

A Board worker node runs no example-hub sync, so kanban_block(needs=[...]) there found no holder
(no hub.db) and answered no_capability_holder; worker-1 run 10113 of MacBook card
t_01a18b13ee350599 then asked David to run the Mac tests by hand.

- route(): without a replica, a copied card parks on the same capability-owner ids, relayed to its
  home gateway (created_on); the home's wake probe (owner_status) routes it with its own registry:
  create-task to a remote holder, or a local owner card (idempotency_key = request id, runs_on
  machine:<home>) when the home holds the need. A worker node's own card gets
  capability_registry_unavailable instead of a misleading no_capability_holder.
- A holder record that lapsed recently (restart/sleep) parks and retries for RELAY_RETRY_S instead
  of refusing; after the window the card wakes with the typed error. Hours-old data still refuses.
- human_request lint: agent_route_gap refuses 'run X and paste results' asks justified by a failed
  agent route; agent_relay_ask also matches 'from a Hermes chat there'.
- Placement on a worker node says it has no replica and names the needs= route.
